  "id": "isolation-experiment",
  "term": "isolation experiment",
  "definition": "An isolation experiment is a study condition in which the target items are presented alone rather than embedded in a larger context such as a sentence. In the source study, written items were shown in isolation so their learning could be compared with learning when the same kinds of items appeared within sentences.",
